      69→
      70→| Check | Description | Expected Result |
      71→|-------|-------------|-----------------|
      72→| E2E script exits 0 | Script completes successfully | PASS |
      73→| `.cast` file created | File exists in `snake/screenshots/` | PASS |
      74→| `.cast` file non-empty | `test -s` returns true (size > 0) | PASS |
      75→| `.cast` file is asciinema format | First character is `{` (JSON header) | PASS |
      76→| `.cast` file has JSON header | File starts with `{"version": 2,` | PASS |
      77→
      78→**v4 Fix**: The `e2e-screenshot.sh` now uses `asciinema rec` to produce proper `.cast` files (asciinema v2 format) instead of `script` which produces typescript format. The script also validates that the output file starts with a JSON header (`{`) to ensure it's valid asciinema format.
